        "type": "text",
        "text": "Glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) is a hormone consisting of 31 amino acids. It is secreted by specialised intestinal epithelial cells known as L cells.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 16
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Fig. 6.1 outlines the secretion of GLP-1 and its effects on the pancreas, brain and stomach.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 16
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "figure",
        "id": "fig6.1",
        "caption": "Fig. 6.1",
        "src": "figures/q6_fig6_1.png",
        "alt": "Flow chart of ingested food, stomach emptying, intestinal L-cell secretion of GLP-1 and effects on the brain, appetite, pancreatic alpha and beta cells and stomach emptying.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 16
        }
      }
    ],
